From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:25:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ifc): export closed sketch loops as IFC profile
 definitions (#26)

Add utilities/ifc_export.py, which writes closed 2D loops as IFC4
IfcArbitraryClosedProfileDef (AREA) entities through ifcopenshell.

ifcopenshell is optional. The module imports without it, and only the
writer needs it, raising IfcOpenShellMissing when it is absent.
closed_loop_points() drops a repeated closing point and rejects
non-finite coordinates and loops with fewer than three distinct points.

testing/test_ifc_export.py covers the loop validation without
ifcopenshell, and a write/re-open round trip that is skipped when
ifcopenshell is missing.
